    "narrative": "The slate today is headlined by **Mickey Moniak**, whose score of 75.98 makes him our most efficient play by a wide margin. **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive 14% park factor boost and a favorable platoon matchup against Sasaki, with the added benefit of a slow pitcher delivery window providing an 88% probability for a stolen base\u2014our primary scarcity target. **Isaac Paredes** follows as our secondary anchor with a 64.31 score, leveraging an elite platoon advantage against Ure\u00f1a and a premium spot in the three-hole. While **Corbin Carroll** and **Seiya Suzuki** also grade out well, **Corbin Carroll** faces a tougher matchup against Tolle, requiring careful monitoring of the wind conditions which are currently projected to offer some assistance. \n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Austin Riley** on the bench despite a respectable 54.15 score. While **Austin Riley** offered potential value against Bradley, his spot in the eight-hole and a lower comparative efficiency against our active utility starters like **Josh Naylor** (60.48) forced him to the pine to maximize our daily cap usage. We must also exercise caution with **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Max Muncy** today; both carry a 42% rain risk that could potentially shorten their outings or affect plate discipline in damp conditions. Furthermore, while **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll** are locked into the lineup, the 3.41 xERA of Tolle suggests they have the narrowest margins for error among our projected starters. We are opting to keep **Zach McKinstry** and **Travis Bazzana** benched due to poor matchups against Skenes and Wilkinson respectively, keeping them well below our 40.0 efficiency floor.",
